 "notes": [
  "All top-level rects are absolute source/layout pixels; template part rects are relative to the instance origin.",
  "Template instances carry {at, data}; a part with \"bind\" takes its asset or text from data[bind].",
  "Tier frames (inventory/frame_<tier>) are the same 140x140 rect as the paintings: use as NinePatch with draw_center=false, margin per tier (legendary 18, others 10); the painting interior is rect [8,8,124,124] inside the crop (border ~5 px + 4 px glow margin; legendary border ~12 px).",
  "Each items/<slug> painting from a card is 140x140 and carries its own tier frame and the Lv badge plate (text erased). The three equipped paintings are 221x194 landscape (y 320..514) with a gold frame, badge plate (text erased) and the red gem; they stop 1 px above the baked name's ascenders.",
  "Filter chips: only ALL has an active state in the reference. To activate any chip, draw inventory/chip_frame_active (NinePatch, margin 14) at that chip's rect and render its label in white title font; draw inventory/chip_frame_idle (NinePatch, margin 14) + the label in its tier colour for an idle ALL.",
  "Chip label colours (sampled): all #FFFFFF, common #FFFFFF, uncommon #BCFF7D, rare #B1ECFF, epic #FFD4FF, legendary #FFFFEA, mystic #EFD6FF, special #FFDAD0.",
  "Card rows in the reference sit at y = 731, 941, 1151, 1362 (pitch 210); columns at x = 162 and 548. The list scrolls; the bottom foliage strip is static under it.",
  "Text sizes are EB Garamond (body) / Cinzel (title) point sizes that reproduce the reference glyph widths; cap_h is the measured capital height in px (the invariant to match if another face is used).",
  "Reference text extents: equipped name x218-377 y520-552 (centred in slot), equipped stat y553-575, card name x318-425 y748-769, card type y778-789, stat lines y812-825 / y840-854, Lv badge text x240-284 y849-861, chip label cap 14 px."
 ],
